-- title:
--   Coefficient Frobenius carries a moduli place to the Frobenius twist
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field, $q'$ a prime with $\operatorname{char}\kappa = q'$, and $N \geq 1$. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC` $\kappa\,N$ for the intermediate field of $\kappa(\!(q)\!)$ over $\kappa$ generated by the expansions `qExpand` $\kappa\,d$ (`jqModC` $\kappa$) for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$. Let $\sigma$ be an element of `SemilinearAut` $\kappa\,F$, that is a pair consisting of a ring automorphism of $F$ and a ring automorphism of $\kappa$ intertwined by the structure map, and assume that $\sigma$ acts on Laurent expansions coefficientwise by the $q'$-power map: for every $x \in F$, the expansion of $\sigma \bullet x$ is the image of that of $x$ under `coeffMap` applied to the ring homomorphism $a \mapsto a^{q'}$ of $\kappa$. Let $x$ be a point of `ModuliPoint` $N\,\kappa$, i.e. a class of pairs consisting of a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with invertible discriminant together with a point of exact additive order $N$, modulo variable changes combined with replacing the generator by a multiple by an integer coprime to $N$. Let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $\kappa$ (a valuation subring containing $\kappa$, distinct from $F$ and a principal ideal ring), and suppose `IsModuliPlaceOf` $\kappa\,N\,x\,v$: there is a field $\Omega$ over $\kappa$ and a `ModuliTestDatum` $\kappa\,N\,x\,\Omega$ — a place $W$ of $\Omega$ over $\kappa$, a Weierstrass curve over the valuation ring of $W$ whose reduction has nonzero discriminant, a point of exact order $N$ on the curve over $\Omega$, a retraction of the residue field onto $\kappa$ splitting the structure map and identifying the reduced pair with $x$, and a $\kappa$-embedding $F \to \Omega$ pinned by the requirement that each generator `jqNFull` $\kappa\,N\,d$ goes to the $j$-invariant of the quotient of the curve by the subgroup generated by $(N/d)$ times the chosen point — whose valuation ring pulls back along that embedding to the valuation ring of $v$. The conclusion is that $\sigma \bullet v$, the transport of $v$ along $\sigma$, satisfies `IsModuliPlaceOf` $\kappa\,N$ for the point `ModuliPoint.map` (`frobenius` $\kappa\,q'$) $x$, obtained by raising the Weierstrass coefficients and the coordinates of the generator to the $q'$-th power.
--
--   This is the compatibility of the Frobenius twist on the moduli side with the coefficientwise $q'$-power map on $q$-expansions: the geometric Frobenius of the characteristic-$q'$ fibre of the level-$N$ modular curve, read through the dictionary between places of the modular function field and pairs (elliptic curve, point of order $N$). It feeds the identification of the valuation ring of the Frobenius operator on places at geometric level with the pullback of the moduli place of the twisted point.
